      "problem": "The lateral surface area of a cube is $400\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
      "worked_solution": "The lateral surface area ${S}_{L}$ of a cube is made up of $4$ congruent squares. So, the area $A$ of one face is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{S}_{L}}{4}=\\frac{400}{4}=100\\,{\\text{ft}}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nSince $A={s}^{2},$ where $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt{A}=\\sqrt{100}=10\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $10\\,\\text{ft}.$",
